<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis offers unchanged, quiet.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis offers unchanged, quiet.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis offers in cash soymeal markets were mostly unchanged in quiet dealings, brokers said.</p>
<p>Prices continued firm on near-term tight meal supplies and many brokers were said to be out of meal until December.</p>
<p>&quot;Everything remains really tight on the supply side,&quot; one river broker said. &quot;As long as the exports hold up, the market should stay that way.&quot;</p>
<p>Citing high prices, South Korea passed overnight on a 70,000 tonne soymeal tender. Some brokers interpreted the cancelled tender as one of the first signs of demand rationing in the export market.</p>
<p>&quot;That could be a sign that things are softening a little bit,&quot; one broker said. &quot;Maybe we're beginning to price ourselves out of business.&quot;  </p>
